--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/audits/MARKET_ROSTER_RELEVANCE_2248.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Market movement linked to prepared roster needs — build 2248
+
+## Confirmed gap and existing systems
+
+Matched disposable 1-QB/K/DEF and Superflex replays on production source build2247 show canonical +150 Market movement and a current prepared RB need, but no personalized Market join. This is source-compatible fixture acceptance, not owner live coverage. The existing Market engine, CheckpointPipeline, sparse store, current_comparison, prepared_diagnostics, prepared_need, ownership resolver and Trade For workspace are reused. No new score, provider acquisition, persistent opportunity engine or runtime owner is introduced.
+
+## Evidence and bounded reads
+
+The Market page reuses its bounded prepared search/directory and canonical trend batch. The new section examines the first ten assets, shows at most three in existing order and prefers position-matched other-owned players when the current prepared need supports them. Exact finite movement zero remains supported. Missing/incompatible dated evidence stays unknown. The dates, current canonical source qualification and endpoint age describe sparse observations, never a continuous daily series or urgency.
+
+Roster diagnostics are requalified by the existing week/scoring/generation, current availability, aging and failed-refresh rules. A starter/depth position match is not a player-specific legal-lineup improvement. Provisional/missing roster evidence retains neutral information and explains why relevance cannot be established. A quote is a neutral index cost, not an acceptance probability or manager asking price. Saved franchise goals, Custom prices and Trade qualification do not change canonical movement.
+
+## Handoff and state
+
+The existing team_need query carries an evidence hash, not authorization. Trade For rechecks the existing active manager membership, exact league/franchise, prepared need, native player position, canonical quote identity and ownership. Changed or unauthorized evidence applies no new target. Existing contextual navigation and Trade workspace preserve the draft, valuation mode, exact protections, comparison selections and retained result. League/account switches invalidate the evidence binding.
+
+The new Market-origin marker suppresses automatic targeted discovery for this handoff only; the existing editable controls and explicit Generate remain. Opening Market, a disclosure or Trade For does not acquire sources, compute lineups, synchronize or evaluate. Personalized text and tokens are inserted after both shared HTML caches, avoiding account-specific retention in those caches.
+
+## Controls and limits
+
+Focused real-route tests cover positive/negative/zero movement, zero current price, incompatible/missing history, mismatched asset identity, availability changes, aging, failed refresh, quote generation and ownership changes, account/league scope and signed-out replay. Browser controls use prepared source-compatible 1-QB/K/DEF and Superflex fixtures at 320x432, 375x667, 390x844 and desktop, keyboard disclosures, touch emulation, exact target and full Back/reload draft/protection/comparison/result preservation. Provider and lineup preparation calls raise if navigation invokes them. Physical iPhone/Safari and authenticated owner live coverage require separate acceptance.
+
+All mandatory local/canonical/hosted results must be recorded for the exact final candidate before release. Development failures remain separate original logs; they are not final-source acceptance. No Trade reserve, FOIS reserve, restoration allowance, scoring/price formula, threshold, account data or submitted lineup changes.
+
+## Reconciled Market-only and warm-cache boundaries
+
+The full regression exposed a Market-only runtime with no projection owner. Personalized lookup now stops with a specific missing-preparation explanation while neutral movement remains visible. The existing multi-account/concurrent-reader control also required one directory read per warm publication; the final path caches the HTML with a small neutral sample in the same bounded byte caches. It adds no cache or runtime owner, and binds personalized context only after retrieval. A historical comparison whose current endpoint is incompatible remains neutral; it cannot supply the personalized Trade For action. Original failed and interrupted candidate evidence is retained separately.
